hadiths[152]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22884","Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us: Mansur, meaning Ibn ZadHan, informed us, from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn Mabad az-Zimmani, from Abu Qatadah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about fasting the day of Arafah, so he said: An expiation of two years. And he was asked about fasting the day of Ashura, so he said: An expiation of a year."
"22885","Hushaym narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Abu Muhammad, a companion who was of Abu Qatadah, who said: Abu Qatadah narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever establishes proof over a slain one, his spoils are his."
"22886","Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal Abu Ismail narrated to us, from Abdur-Rahman, meaning Ibn Ishaq, from Zayd ibn Abi Attab, from Amr ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abu Qatadah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was praying, carrying Umamah, or Umaymah, the daughter of Abu al-As, and she is the daughter of Zaynab; he would carry her when he stood and put her down when he bowed, until he finished."
"22887","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Hisham ad-Dastuwai narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would lead us, reciting to us in the first two rakahs of the noon prayer, and would let us hear a verse sometimes, and would lengthen the first and shorten the second, and would do that in the dawn prayer, lengthening the first and shortening the second, and would recite to us in the first two rakahs of the afternoon prayer."
"22888","Abdul-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from Abu Qatadah, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that anything of it be mixed with anything, but each one of them should be infused separately."
"22889","Abdul-Wahhab ath-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade breathing into the vessel, or touching his penis with his right hand, or cleaning himself with his right hand."
"22890","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Malik, meaning Ibn Anas, narrated to us, from Amir ibn Abdullah, meaning Ibn az-Zubayr, from Amr ibn Sulaym, from Abu Qatadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him bow two rakahs before he sits."
"22891","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Malik narrated to us, from Amir ibn Abdullah, from Amr ibn Sulaym, from Abu Qatadah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray while carrying Umamah the daughter of Zaynab; when he bowed and prostrated, he put her down, and when he stood, he carried her."
"22892","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, who said: I used to see a dream that would make me shiver from it, except that I would not be wrapped, until I met Abu Qatadah. So I mentioned that to him, so he narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: A good dream is from Allah, and a bad dream is from Satan. So whoever sees a dream he dislikes, let him not inform of it, and let him spit to his left three times, and let him seek refuge in Allah from its evil, for indeed it will not harm him. Sufyan said another time: For indeed he will never see anything he dislikes."
"22893","Sufyan narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, who heard it from Abu Muhammad, who heard it from Abu Qatadah: He hit a wild donkey, meaning while he was in ihram release and they were in ihram, so they asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he commanded them to eat it."
"22894","Sufyan narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Abu Muhammad, the companion of Abu Qatadah, from Abu Qatadah, who said: I duelled a man on the day of Hunayn, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave me his spoils."
"22895","Sufyan narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to me: The wife of Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to me that Abu Qatadah would tilt the vessel for the cat to drink, and said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to us that it is not impure; indeed it is of those that go around you, males and females."
"22896","Sufyan narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman and Ibn Ajlan, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr, from Amr ibn Sulaym, from Abu Qatadah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him pray two rakahs before he sits."
"22897","Sufyan narrated to us, who said: We heard it from Dawud ibn Shabur, from Abu Qazah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abu Harmalah, from Abu Qatadah, who said: Fasting Arafah expiates the year and the one following it, and fasting Ashura expiates a year. Sufyan did not raise it for us, and it is raised."
"22898","Abdullah narrated to us: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, and he said: From the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"22899","Sufyan narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman and Ibn Ajlan, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr, from Amr ibn Sulaym, from Abu Qatadah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, leading the people, with Umamah the daughter of Abu al-As, meaning carrying her; when he bowed, he put her down, and when he finished prostration, he lifted her."
"22900","Ismail narrated to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the call is made for prayer, do not stand until you see me."
"22901","Ismail narrated to us: al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from Abu Qatadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you drinks, let him not breathe into the vessel, and when he goes to the lavatory, let him not touch his penis with his right hand, and when he wipes himself, let him not wipe himself with his right hand."
"22902","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Harmalah ibn Iyas, from Abu Qatadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The fast of the day of Arafah expiates two years, a past one and a coming one, and the fast of Ashura expiates a past year."
"22903","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Said, meaning Ibn Abi Hind, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah narrated to me, from a son of Kab ibn Malik, from Abu Qatadah ibn Ribi, who said: A funeral passed by the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: One is relieved, and relief is sought from another. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the relieved one and the one relief is sought from? He said: The believer is relieved from the toil of the world and its harm to the mercy of Allah Almighty, and from the wicked one the servants, the lands, the trees, and the beasts find relief."
"22904","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah: Ghaylan ibn Jarir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Mabad al-Zimmani, from Abu Qatadah, who said: Shubah said: I said to Ghaylan: The Ansari? So he nodded his head, meaning yes: A man asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about his fasting, so he became angry, and Umar said: I am pleased, or he said: We are pleased, with Allah as Lord and with Islam as religion, and I do not know but that he said: And with Muhammad as Messenger, and with our pledge as a pledge. He said: Then Umar, or another man, stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man who fasts perpetually? He said: He neither fasted nor broke fast, or: He did not fast and did not break fast. He said: Fasting two days and breaking one day? He said: And who can bear that? He said: Breaking two days and fasting one day? He said: Would that Allah Almighty gave us strength for that. He said: Fasting one day and breaking one day? He said: That is the fast of my brother Dawud. He said: Fasting Monday and Thursday? He said: That is a day in which I was born and in which revelation came down upon me. He said: Fasting three days of every month, and Ramadan to Ramadan, is the fast of the whole year and its breaking. He said: The fast of the day of Arafah? He said: It expiates the past year and the remaining one. He said: The fast of the day of Ashura? He said: It expiates the past year."
"22905","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us: A son of Kab ibn Malik narrated to me, from Abu Qatadah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying upon this minbar: O people, beware of narrating much from me; whoever speaks about me, let him speak only truth or correctness, for whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"22906","Waki narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to let us hear a verse sometimes in Zuhr and Asr."
"22907","Waki narrated to us: Abu al-Umays narrated to us, from Amir, meaning Ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Zuraqi, from Abu Qatadah: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he sat in prayer, placed his right hand upon his right thigh and pointed with his finger."
"22908","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Abdullah ibn Mabad al-Zimmani, from Abu Qatadah al-Ansari: A Bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about his fasting, and he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: The fast of Monday? He said: That is a day in which I was born and in which revelation came down upon me."
"22909","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said informed us that Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi informed him that Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah informed him that his father used to narrate that a man asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: O Messenger of Allah, what if I am killed in the path of Allah, patient, seeking reward, advancing, not retreating, will Allah expiate my sins by it? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you are killed in the path of Allah, patient, seeking reward, advancing, not retreating, Allah will expiate your sins by it. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, waited as long as Allah willed, then the man asked him: O Messenger of Allah, if I am killed in the path of Allah, advancing, not retreating, will Allah expiate my sins? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you are killed in the path of Allah, advancing, not retreating, Allah will expiate your sins, except debt; thus Jibril, peace be upon him, said to me."
"22910","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: A funeral was brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for him to pray over it, so he said: Is there a debt upon him? They said: Yes, two dinars. He said: Did he leave payment for them? They said: No. He said: Pray over your companion. Abu Qatadah said: They are upon me, O Messenger of Allah. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed over him."
"22911","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Mabad ibn Kab ibn Malik, from Abu Qatadah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Beware of frequent oaths in selling, for it sells the goods then wipes out the blessing."
"22912","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq: Mabad ibn Kab ibn Malik narrated to me that he heard Abu Qatadah al-Sulami narrating that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Beware of frequent oaths in selling, for it sells the goods then wipes out the blessing."
"22913","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Abu Qatadah, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and he said: If you do not reach water tomorrow, you will thirst. The hasty people went off seeking water, while I stayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The mount of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, inclined, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, dozed, so I supported him, then he leaned again and I supported him, then he leaned until he almost fell from his mount, so I supported him and he woke and said: Who is the man? I said: Abu Qatadah. He said: How long has your journey been? I said: Since the night. He said: May Allah protect you as you protected His Messenger. Then he said: If only we halted to rest. So he inclined toward a tree and dismounted and said: Look, do you see anyone? I said: This is a rider, these are two riders, until they reached seven. He said: Guard our prayer for us. So we slept, and nothing woke us but the heat of the sun. We awoke, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rode and we rode a little, then he dismounted and said: Do you have water? I said: Yes, with me is a water-skin with some water in it. He said: Bring it. I brought it to him, and he said: Touch lightly from it, touch lightly from it. The people performed ablution, and a draught remained, so he said: Preserve it, O Abu Qatadah, for it will have a story. Then Bilal called the adhan, and they prayed the two rakahs before Fajr, then they prayed Fajr. Then he rode and we rode, and some said to others: We were negligent concerning our prayer. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What are you saying? If it is a matter of your world, it is your affair, but if it is a matter of your religion, then it is for me. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we were negligent concerning our prayer. He said: There is no negligence in sleep; negligence is only in wakefulness. If that happens, pray it, and the next day at its time. Then he said: Think about the people. They said: You said yesterday: If you do not reach water tomorrow, you will thirst, so the people are at the water. He said: The people woke and missed their Prophet. Some said to others: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is at the water, and among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar, and they said: O people, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not go ahead of you to the water and leave you behind; if the people obey Abu Bakr and Umar, they will be guided; he said it three times. When the midday heat intensified, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, appeared to them, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, we are perishing of thirst, our necks are cut off. He said: No ruin upon you. Then he said: O Abu Qatadah, bring the water-skin. I brought it to him, and he said: Loosen my cup for me, meaning his cup, so I loosened it and brought it to him, and he poured into it and gave the people to drink. The people crowded upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O people, behave well in the crowd, for each of you will leave satisfied. The people drank until none remained but me and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He poured for me and said: Drink, O Abu Qatadah. I said: You drink, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The cupbearer of the people is the last of them. So I drank, and he drank after me, and there remained in the water-skin about what had been in it, and they that day were three hundred. Abdullah said: Imran ibn Husayn heard me narrating this hadith in the congregational mosque and said: Who is the man? I said: I am Abdullah ibn Rabah al-Ansari. He said: The people know their hadith best; see how you narrate, for I was one of the seven that night. When I finished, he said: I did not think anyone remembered this hadith besides me. Hammad said: And Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Abu Qatadah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it, and he added: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he halted at night with night still upon him, pillowed his right side, and when he halted near morning, he placed his head upon his right palm and set up his forearm."
"22914","Abdullah narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Abu Qatadah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"22915","Abdullah narrated to us: Ibrahim narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Bakr ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Abu Qatadah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"22916","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, who said: We were with Abu Qatadah on the roof of our house, and he saw a shooting star fall, and they looked at it, so Abu Qatadah said: We have been forbidden to follow it with our gazes."
"22917","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Abdullah ibn Mabad, from Abu Qatadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the fast of Monday, and he said: In it I was born, and in it revelation came down upon me."
"22918","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Sumayr, who said: Abdullah ibn Rabah came to us, and I found people gathered to him. He said: Abu Qatadah, the horseman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent the army of the commanders and said: Upon you is Zayd ibn Harithah; if Zayd is struck, then Jafar; if Jafar is struck, then Abdullah ibn Rawahah al-Ansari. Jafar leapt up and said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Prophet of Allah, I did not fear that you would appoint Zayd over me. He said: Proceed, for you do not know which of that is better. The army set out and stayed as long as Allah willed. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ascended the minbar and ordered that it be announced: Prayer in congregation. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Good news has come, or: Good has returned, Abd al-Rahman doubted: Shall I not inform you of this raiding army of yours? They set out until they met the enemy, and Zayd was struck a martyr, so seek forgiveness for him, and the people sought forgiveness for him. Then Jafar ibn Abi Talib took the banner and pressed upon the enemy until he was killed a martyr; I testify to him of martyrdom, so seek forgiveness for him. Then Abdullah ibn Rawahah took the banner and planted his feet until he was struck a martyr, so seek forgiveness for him. Then Khalid ibn al-Walid took the banner, though he was not of the commanders; he appointed himself. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his two fingers and said: O Allah, he is a sword of Your swords, so grant him victory. And Abd al-Rahman once said: Grant victory through him. On that day Khalid was named the Sword of Allah. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Go forth and reinforce your brothers, and let none stay behind. So the people went forth in severe heat, on foot and mounted."
"22919","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Rufay, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not curse time, for Allah is Time."
"22920","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us: Haywah narrated to us: Abu Sakhr Humayd ibn Ziyad narrated to us that Yahya ibn al-Nadr narrated to him, from Abu Qatadah, that he was present at that: Amr ibn al-Jamuh came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I fight in the path of Allah until I am killed, shall I walk with this leg of mine sound in Paradise? And his leg was lame. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Yes. They were killed on the day of Uhud, he and his nephew and their freedman. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by him and said: As if I look at you walking with this leg of yours sound in Paradise. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered concerning them and their freedman, and they were placed in one grave."
"22921","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, that he witnessed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying over a dead person, and I heard him saying: O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our present and our absent, our young and our old, our male and our female. Yahya said: And Abu Salamah added in it: O Allah, whomever of us You keep alive, keep him alive upon Islam, and whomever of us You take, take him upon faith."
"22922","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from his father: Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah narrated to me, from his father: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he was called for a funeral, asked about it; if it was praised with good, he stood and prayed over it, and if other than that was said of it, he said to its family: Deal with it yourselves, and he did not pray over it."
"22923","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, and he mentioned the like of it."
"22924","Said, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sits upon the bed of an absent wife, Allah will appoint for him on the Day of Resurrection a serpent."
"22925","Abu Said narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Usayd, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever abandons Friday three times without necessity, a seal is placed upon his heart."
"22926","Yunus and Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Affan said in his hadith: Abu Jafar al-Khatmi informed us, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Abu Qatadah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever relieves his debtor, or remits it from him, will be in the shade of the Throne on the Day of Resurrection."
"22927","Hasan ibn Musa and Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abu Qatadah, that he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, urinating facing the qiblah."
"22928","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: My father said: Ishaq, meaning Ibn al-Tabba, narrated to us the like of it, saying: Abu Qatadah informed me."
"22929","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, and Yahya ibn Ishaq said: Ibn Lahiah informed us; Hasan said in his hadith: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Ali ibn Rabah, from Abu Qatadah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The best horses are the dark bay with a white blaze on the forehead and white on the upper lip, with three legs marked white and the right foreleg unmarked; if it is not dark bay, then a dark red horse of this coloring."
"22930","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar, from Ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sits upon the bed of an absent wife, a serpent will be raised up for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"22931","Yunus narrated to us: Aban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to lead us in prayer, reciting in Asr and Zuhr, in the first two rakahs, two surahs along with the Mother of the Book, and he used to let us hear a verse sometimes, and he recited in the last two rakahs the Mother of the Book, and he used to lengthen the first rakah of the Fajr prayer and the first rakah of the Zuhr prayer."
"22932","Abu al-Mughirah and Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, saying: al-Awzai narrated to us: Yahya narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The righteous dream is from Allah, and the bad dream is from Satan; if one of you dreams a dream he fears, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge with Allah from Satan, for it will not harm him."
"22933","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: al-Awzai narrated to us: Ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah al-Ansari: My father narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When one of you urinates, let him not touch his penis with his right hand, nor clean himself with his right hand, nor breathe into the vessel."
"22934","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Sumayr, who said: Abdullah ibn Rabah al-Ansari came to us, and the Ansar used to consider him learned, so I went to him while he was in the tent of Sharik ibn al-Awar overlooking the Mirbad, with people gathered to him, and he said: Abu Qatadah al-Ansari, the horseman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent the army of the commanders and said: Upon you is Zayd ibn Harithah; if Zayd is struck, then Jafar ibn Abi Talib; if Jafar is struck, then Abdullah ibn Rawahah al-Ansari. Jafar leapt up and said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, I did not fear that you would appoint Zayd over me. He said: Proceed, for you do not know which of that is better. They set out and stayed as long as Allah willed. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ascended the minbar and ordered that it be announced: Prayer in congregation. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Good news has come, or: It has spent the night well, or: Good has returned, Abd al-Rahman doubted: Shall I not inform you of this raiding army of yours? They set out and met the enemy, and Zayd was struck a martyr, so seek forgiveness for him, and the people sought forgiveness for him. Then Jafar ibn Abi Talib took the banner and pressed upon the enemy until he was killed a martyr; I testify to him of martyrdom, so seek forgiveness for him. Then Abdullah ibn Rawahah took the banner and planted his feet until he was killed a martyr, so seek forgiveness for him. Then Khalid ibn al-Walid took the banner, though he was not of the commanders; he appointed himself. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his two fingers and said: O Allah, he is a sword of Your swords, so grant him victory. From that day Khalid was named the Sword of Allah. Then he said: Go forth and reinforce your brothers, and let none stay behind. The people went forth in severe heat, on foot and mounted."
"22935","I read to Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi: Malik, from Abi al-Nadr, the freedman of Umar ibn Ubaydullah, from Nafi, the freedman of Abu Qatadah al-Ansari, from Abu Qatadah, that he was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until when they were on one of the roads of Mecca, he stayed behind with companions of his who were in ihram while he was not in ihram. He saw a wild donkey, mounted his horse, and asked his companions to hand him his whip, but they refused; he asked them for his spear, but they refused, and he took it, then charged the donkey and killed it. Some of the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ate, and some refused. When they reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, they asked him about that, and he said: It is but food Allah Almighty fed you with."
"22936","I read to Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi: Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Qatadah, concerning the wild donkey, the like of that, except that in the hadith of Zayd ibn Aslam the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Is any of its meat with you?"
"22937","Ismail narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered ihram in the year of Hudaybiyah, while Abu Qatadah did not enter ihram. It was reported to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that there was an enemy at Fiqa, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out. While I was with my companions, some of them laughed to others, so I looked, and there was a wild donkey. I sought their help, but they refused to help me, so I charged it and brought it down. We ate of its meat, and we feared being cut off, so I went seeking the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raising my horse to a gallop then riding at a walk. I met a man of Banu Ghifar in the depth of night and said: Where did you leave the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: I left him at Tihan, toward Suqya. I reached him and said: O Messenger of Allah, your companions send you greeting and the mercy of Allah, and they feared being cut off without you, so wait for them. He said: So he waited for them. I said: I obtained a wild donkey, and I have some of it left. He said to the people: Eat, while they were in ihram."
"22938","Ismail narrated to us: Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite with us in the first two rakahs of the Zuhr prayer, letting us hear a verse sometimes, lengthening the first and shortening the second, and he used to do that in the Fajr prayer, lengthening the first and shortening the second, and he used to recite with us in the first two rakahs of the Asr prayer."
"22939","Ismail narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Mabad ibn Kab ibn Malik narrated to me, from Abu Qatadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Beware of frequent oaths in selling, for it sells the goods then wipes out the blessing."
"22940","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, saying: I heard Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab narrating, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a man of the Ansar to pray over him, and he said: Pray over your companion, for there is a debt upon him. Abu Qatadah said: It is upon me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: With full payment? He said: With full payment. So he prayed over him; it was only eighteen or nineteen dirhams."
"22941","Bahz narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab informed me, saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah narrating from his father, and he mentioned the like of it, except that he said: Abu Qatadah said: I guarantee it. He said: With full payment? And Hajjaj also said: I guarantee it; and he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah."
"22942","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, saying: I heard Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab, saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah narrating from his father Abu Qatadah that they were on a journey of theirs, and I saw a wild donkey, so I rode a horse and took the spear and killed it. Among us was one in ihram. They ate of it, then they feared. I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked. He said: Did you point, or help, or hunt? Shubah said: I do not know whether he said: Did you help, or did you hunt? Then they said: No. So he ordered them to eat it."
"22943","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Abu Qatadah al-Ansari, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on one of his journeys, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, inclined, or he said: Turned aside, from his mount, so I supported him with my hands. He awoke. Then we traveled, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, inclined, so I supported him with my hands, and he awoke. Abu Qatadah said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: May Allah protect you as you protected us since the night. Then he said: I think we have burdened you; turn us aside from the road, or: Incline us from the road. So we turned aside from the road, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made his mount kneel. Each man of us pillowed the foreleg of his mount. We did not wake until the sun shone, and he mentioned the sound of the shrike. I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are ruined, the prayer escaped us. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You are not ruined, and the prayer did not escape you; it escapes only the wakeful, not the sleeper. Is there water? I brought him a flat vessel, or he said: A water-skin, with water in it. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution, then handed it to me, with a remainder of water in it. He said: Guard it, for it will have a story. He ordered Bilal, who called the adhan, and he prayed two rakahs, then moved in his place, ordered him, and he called the iqamah, and he prayed the Fajr prayer. Then the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If the people obeyed Abu Bakr and Umar, they treated themselves gently and were right, and if they opposed them, they harmed themselves. Abu Bakr and Umar, when they missed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to the people: Stay at the water until morning, but they refused them. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reached them at the end of the day, when they were almost perishing of thirst. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we are perishing. He called for the water-skin, then called for a vessel, and a vessel larger than a cup and smaller than a bowl was brought. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, held the two under his arm, then poured into the vessel, and the people drank until all drank. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called: Is there any withholder? Then he returned the water-skin with about what had been in it. We asked him: How many were you? He said: With Abu Bakr and Umar were eighty men, and with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, we were twelve men."
"22944","Ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah narrated to me, from Mabad ibn Kab ibn Malik, that Abu Qatadah, my father informed him, and Yazid ibn Harun said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Mabad ibn Kab ibn Malik, from Abu Qatadah, to the same meaning, saying: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a gathering, when a funeral passed by. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Relieved, and relief sought from him. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the relieved one? He said: The believing servant is relieved from the toil of the world and its harm to the mercy of Allah. We said: Then what is the one relief is sought from? He said: The wicked servant; from him the servants, the lands, the trees, and the beasts find relief."
"22945","Ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah narrated to me, from Mabad ibn Kab ibn Malik, that Abu Qatadah, my father informed him, and Yazid ibn Harun said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Mabad ibn Kab ibn Malik, from Abu Qatadah, to the same meaning, saying: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a gathering, when a funeral passed by. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Relieved, and relief sought from him. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the relieved one? He said: The believing servant is relieved from the toil of the world and its harm to the mercy of Allah. We said: Then what is the one relief is sought from? He said: The wicked servant; from him the servants, the lands, the trees, and the beasts find relief."
"22946","Abd al-Rahman said: And I read it to Malik, meaning this hadith."
"22947","Ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Abu Qatadah: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The cupbearer of the people is the last of them."
"22948","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Malik narrated to us, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Amr ibn Sulaym, from Abu Qatadah; Abd al-Razzaq said in his hadith: He said: I heard Abu Qatadah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him bow two rakahs before he sits."
"22949","Abd al-Rahman and Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Malik narrated to us, from Amir ibn Abdullah, from Amr ibn Sulaym, from Abu Qatadah; Abd al-Razzaq said in his hadith: He said: I heard Abu Qatadah saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, carrying Umamah, the daughter of Zaynab; Abd al-Razzaq said: Upon his shoulder. When he bowed and prostrated, he put her down, and when he stood, he carried her."
"22950","I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq, meaning Ibn Isa, narrated to us: Malik informed me, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Humaydah, the daughter of Ubayd ibn Rifah, from Kabshah, the daughter of Kab ibn Malik; Ishaq said in his hadith: She was under the son of Abu Qatadah: Abu Qatadah came to her, and she poured his ablution water for him. A cat came drinking from it, so he tilted the vessel for it until it drank. Kabshah said: He saw me looking at him, and he said: Do you wonder, O daughter of my brother? She said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is not impure; it is of those that go around you, male and female. And Ishaq said: Or the females."
"22951","Ismail narrated to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the call is made for prayer, do not stand until you see me."
"22952","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, that he heard Abdullah ibn Mabad al-Zimmani narrating from Abu Qatadah: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about his fasting, so he became angry, and Umar said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger, and he mentioned the hadith."
"22953","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Abd Rabb, and Hajjaj said: From Abd Rabbihi, from Abu Salamah, who said: I used to see a dream that made me ill. He said: Then I met Abu Qatadah, and he said: I too used to see a dream that made me ill, until I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The righteous dream is from Allah; when one of you sees what he loves, let him narrate it only to one he loves, and when he sees what he hates, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge with Allah from Satan the accursed and from its evil, and let him not narrate it to anyone, for it will not harm him. Hajjaj said: Shubah said: So I said to him: To seek refuge with Allah from Satan? He said: Yes."
"22954","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us: Said ibn Abi Said narrated to me, from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi, that he heard Abu Qatadah saying: While we were sitting in the mosque, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us carrying Umamah, the daughter of Abi al-As ibn al-Rabi, whose mother was Zaynab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a young child. He carried her upon his shoulder. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with her upon his shoulder, putting her down when he bowed and returning her to his shoulder when he stood. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with her upon his shoulder until he finished his prayer, doing that with her."
"22955","Hajjaj narrated to us: Layth narrated to us: Said ibn Abi Said narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, that he heard Abu Qatadah narrating from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he stood among them and mentioned to them striving in the path of Allah Almighty and faith in Allah as among the best deeds. A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I am killed in the path of Allah, will my sins be expiated? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Yes, if you are killed in the path of Allah, patient, seeking reward, advancing, not retreating. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: How did you say? He said: What if I am killed in the path of Allah, will my sins be expiated? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Yes, if you are killed, patient, seeking reward, advancing, not retreating, except debt, for Jibril, peace be upon him, said that to me."
"22956","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: A funeral was brought to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for him to pray over it, and he said: Is there a debt upon him? They said: Yes, two dinars. He said: Did he leave payment for them? They said: No. He said: Pray over your companion. Abu Qatadah said: They are upon me, O Messenger of Allah. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed over him."
"22957","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: A funeral was brought to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for him to pray over it, and he said: Is there a debt upon him? They said: Yes, two dinars. He said: Did he leave payment for them? They said: No. He said: Pray over your companion. Abu Qatadah said: They are upon me, O Messenger of Allah. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed over him."
"22958","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Harmalah ibn Iyas al-Shaybani, from Abu Qatadah: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The fast of the day of Arafah is expiation for two years, a past year and a coming year, and the fast of the day of Ashura is expiation for a year."
"22959","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi, that he heard Abu Qatadah saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with Umamah, the daughter of Zaynab, the daughter of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she being the daughter of Abi al-As ibn al-Rabi ibn Abd al-Uzza, upon his neck. When he bowed, he put her down, and when he rose from his prostration, he took her and returned her to his neck. Amir said: I did not ask him which prayer it was."
"22960","Ibn Jurayj said: And it was narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Abi Attab, from Amr ibn Sulaym, that it was the Fajr prayer. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He did it well."
"22961","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the time of Hudaybiyah. My companions entered ihram, while I did not enter ihram. I saw a donkey, charged it, and hunted it. I mentioned its case to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that I had not entered ihram and that I had hunted it only for you. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered his companions, and they ate, while he did not eat of it when I informed him that I had hunted it for him."
"22962","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, meaning Ibn Abi Talib, informed me, saying: Muawiyah came to Medina, and Abu Qatadah met him and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You will meet after me favoritism. He said: Then with what did he order you? He said: He ordered us to be patient. He said: Then be patient."
"22963","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah al-Dili narrated to me, from Ibn Kab ibn Malik, from Abu Qatadah, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one day, when a funeral passed by him. He said: Relieved, and relief sought from him. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what is relieved and relief sought from? He said: The righteous servant is relieved from the toil of the world and its worry to the mercy of Allah Almighty, and from the wicked servant the servants, the lands, the trees, and the beasts find relief."
"22964","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, who said: I used to suffer severity from dreams, except that I was not wrapped up, until Abu Qatadah narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The dream is from Allah, and the bad dream is from Satan. If one of you dreams a dream he dislikes, let him spit to his left three spits and seek refuge with Allah from Satan, for it will not harm him."
"22965","Sufyan narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman: He heard Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrating, from Amr ibn Sulaym, from Abu Qatadah: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him bow two rakahs before he sits. And Murrah narrated to us, saying: From Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman ibn Ajlan, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, and he mentioned the hadith."
"22966","Makhlad ibn Yazid al-Harrani narrated to us: al-Awzai narrated to us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Qatadah, from his father Abu Qatadah, the horseman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to recite in the first two rakahs of Zuhr and Asr the Opening of the Book and a surah, and in the last two rakahs the Opening of the Book."
"22967","Suwayd ibn Amr al-Kalbi narrated to us: Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to lead us in prayer, reciting in Zuhr and Asr, in the first two, two surahs along with the Mother of the Book, and he used to let us hear a verse sometimes, and in the last two with the Mother of the Book, and he used to lengthen the first rakah of the Zuhr prayer and the Asr prayer."
"22968","And he used to say: When the prayer is established, do not stand until you see me."
"22969","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: al-Awzai narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite the Mother of the Quran and two surahs with it in the two rakahs of the Zuhr and Asr prayers, letting us hear a verse sometimes, and he used to lengthen the first rakah."
"22970","Bishr ibn Shuayb narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from al-Zuhri: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me that Abu Qatadah was of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his horsemen. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The dream is from Allah, and the bad dream is from Satan. When one of you dreams a dream he dislikes, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge with Allah from it, for it will not harm him."
"22971","Hashim narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Abu Qatadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The cupbearer of the people is the last of them."
"22972","Hashim narrated to us: al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Abu Qatadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Negligence is not in sleep; negligence is only in wakefulness."
"22973","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Zaidah narrated to us: Amr ibn Yahya al-Ansari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban narrated to us, from Amr ibn Sulaym ibn Khaldah al-Ansari, from Abu Qatadah, who said: I entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was sitting among the people, so I sat. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What prevented you from bowing two rakahs before you sat? I said: I saw you sitting and the people sitting. He said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him not sit until he bows two rakahs."
"22974","Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak informed us: al-Awzai narrated to me: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: I stand in prayer wanting to lengthen it, then I hear the crying of a child, so I shorten my prayer, disliking to burden his mother."
"22975","Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay narrated to me, from Mujahid, and from Ibn Abi Qatadah, from Abu Qatadah, who said: I was with a group of the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and they were in ihram except one man. He saw game, took a whip, charged it, and caught it. He ate of it, and we ate. Then we took provisions of it. When we came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, we said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so was non-muhrim, and he caught game, and he ate of it, and we ate with him, and we have some of it with us. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them: Eat."
"22976","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq: Mabad ibn Kab ibn Malik narrated to me, from Abu Qatadah al-Harith ibn Ribi, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us to Sayf al-Bahr on one of his Umrahs to Mecca, promising to meet us at Qudayd. We set out, some of us in halal and some in ihram. I was in halal, and he mentioned the hadith. In it: This foreleg, I roasted it, cooked it well, and made it tasty. He said: Bring it. I brought it to him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ate of it while in ihram until he finished it."
"22977","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq: Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah, the freedman of Banu Tamim, narrated to me, from Abu Muhammad Nafi al-Aqra, the freedman of Banu Ghifar, from Abu Qatadah, the like of the hadith of Mabad ibn Kab, neither adding nor omitting."
"22978","Yaqub narrated to us: Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Shihab: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to me that Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever sees me in a dream will see me awake, or: It is as if he saw me awake; Satan does not take my likeness."
"22979","Abu Salamah said: Abu Qatadah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever saw me has seen the truth."
"22980","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me that he narrated from Abu Qatadah."
"22981","My father said: And Ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Said, from Nafi al-Aqra, Abu Muhammad, the freedman of Banu Ghifar, from Abu Qatadah, who said: Abu Qatadah said: I saw two men fighting, a Muslim and a polytheist, and a man of the polytheists wanted to aid his polytheist companion against the Muslim, so I went to him and struck his hand and cut it off. He embraced me with his other hand, and by Allah, he did not release me until I smelled death. Had not blood flowed from him, he would have killed me. He fell, and I struck him and killed him. Fighting diverted me from him, and a man of the people of Mecca passed by him and stripped him. When we finished and war laid down its burdens, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever kills a slain one, his spoils are his. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I killed a slain one, but I was stripped of him, and fighting diverted me from him, and I do not know who stripped him. A man of the people of Mecca said: He spoke truth, O Messenger of Allah; I stripped him, so compensate him from his spoils. Abu Bakr said: Would you go to a lion of the lions of Allah fighting for Allah Almighty and share his spoils? Return to him the spoils of his slain. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He spoke truth, so return to him the spoils of his slain. Abu Qatadah said: So I took it from him, sold it, and bought with its price a garden in Medina, and it was the first wealth I acquired."
"22982","Hasan ibn Musa and Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: While we were praying with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he heard a clamor of men. When he prayed, he called them and said: What is the matter with you? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we hurried to the prayer. He said: Do not do so; when you come to prayer, calmness is upon you. What you reach, pray, and what you miss, complete."
"22983","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Maslamah, who said: I heard Abu Nadrah narrating from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: One better than me informed me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Ammar, when he was digging the trench, wiping his head and saying: Woe to Ibn Sumayyah, the rebellious party will kill you."
"22984","Hasan ibn Yahya of the people of Marw narrated to us: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Maslamah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: One better than me, Abu Qatadah, informed me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Ammar ibn Yasir: The rebellious party will kill you."
"22985","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Ibn al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us: Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah al-Ansari narrated to us, from his father Abu Qatadah, who said: We traveled with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a night journey, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you halted us to rest. He said: I fear you will sleep through prayer; who will wake us for prayer? Bilal said: I, O Messenger of Allah. So he halted the people, and we lay down, and Bilal leaned against his mount, and his eyes overcame him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, awoke with the edge of the sun risen and said: O Bilal, where is what you said to us? I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Him who sent you with truth, no slumber like it was ever cast upon me. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah Almighty took your souls when He willed and returned them to you when He willed. Then he ordered them, and they scattered for their needs and performed ablution. The sun rose, and he led them in Fajr."
"22986","Husayn narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Salih, meaning Ibn Abi Hassan, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him on a scout toward Ghayqah and Waddan, while he was in ihram and Abu Qatadah was not in ihram. A wild donkey appeared; he asked them for a whip, but they did not hand him one, so he snatched the whip of one of them and hunted a wild donkey. They ate it, then joined the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Abwa. They said: We did something we do not know what it is. He said: Feed us."
"22987","Yunus narrated to us: Aban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the prayer is established, do not stand until you see me."
"22988","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Qatadah al-Ansari, that he killed a man of the disbelievers, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave him his spoils and his armor as extra share. He sold it for five uqiyyahs."
"22989","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us: Abu Sakhr informed me that Yahya ibn al-Nadr al-Ansari narrated to him that he heard Abu Qatadah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying upon the minbar to the Ansar: The people are my inner garment, and the Ansar are my outer garment. If the people took a valley and the Ansar took a mountain path, I would follow the mountain path of the Ansar. Had it not been for the Hijrah, I would have been a man of the Ansar. Whoever is put in charge of the Ansar, let him do good to their good-doer and overlook their evil-doer. Whoever frightens them has frightened this which is between these two, and he pointed to himself, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"22990","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, saying: Ata ibn Abi Rabah was asked, while I was present, about the virtue of fasting the day of Arafah, and he said: This came from your direction, O people of Iraq. Abu al-Khalil narrated to me, from Harmalah ibn Iyas, from Abu Qatadah: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said a word resembling its equivalent. He said: The fast of Arafah equals the fast of two years, and the fast of Ashura equals the fast of a year."
"22991","Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah narrated to us, from his father Abu Qatadah: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite in the Zuhr prayer, in the first two rakahs, the Mother of the Book and two surahs, and he used to let us hear a verse sometimes, and he used to recite in the last two rakahs the Mother of the Quran. He used to lengthen the first rakah what he did not lengthen in the second, and likewise in the Asr prayer, and likewise in the Fajr prayer. Affan said: And Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar was exactly the like."
"22992","Affan narrated to us: Aban narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah narrated to me, from his father Abu Qatadah: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade mixing unripe dates with ripe dates, mixing raisins with dates, and mixing ripening dates with fresh dates, for him."
"22993","He said: And Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Abu Qatadah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"22994","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah narrated to us, from his father, that he witnessed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying over a dead person, and I heard him saying: O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our present and our absent, our young and our old, our male and our female."
"22995","He said: And Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me these eight words and added two words: Whomever of us You keep alive, keep him alive upon Islam, and whomever of us You take, take him upon faith."
"22996","Affan narrated to us: Aban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ibrahim, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"22997","Affan narrated to us: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us: Ghaylan ibn Jarir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Mabad al-Zimmani, from Abu Qatadah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: A man said to him: What about the fast of Arafah? He said: I hope with Allah that it expiates the past year and the remaining one. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what about the fast of Ashura? He said: I hope with Allah that it expiates the year."
"22998","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the prayer is established, do not stand until you see me."
"22999","Affan narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us: Abu Jafar al-Khatmi informed us, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, that Abu Qatadah had a debt upon a man, and he used to come to him demanding it, and he hid from him. He came one day, and a boy came out, and he asked him about him. He said: Yes, he is in the house eating khazirah. He called him: O so-and-so, come out, for I have been informed you are here. He came out to him and said: What keeps you from me? He said: I am in hardship, and I have nothing. He said: By Allah, are you in hardship? He said: Yes. Abu Qatadah wept, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever relieves his debtor, or remits it from him, will be in the shade of the Throne on the Day of Resurrection."
"23000","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, who said: I heard a man, Sad said: He was called the freedman of Abu Qatadah, though he was not a freedman, narrating from Abu Qatadah that he obtained a wild donkey, and they asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in ihram. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Is any of it left with you? Shubah said: Then I asked him after, and he said: Is any of it left with you? He said: So he ate it, or he said: So eat it. I said to Shubah: The meaning of his saying: There is no harm in it? He said: Yes."
"23001","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, informed us, he said: I was told, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you recite behind me? They said: Yes. He said: Then do not do so except with the Mother of the Book."
"23002","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said informed us, on the authority of Said al-Maqburi, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, on the authority of his father, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, if I am killed in the path of Allah, patient, seeking reward, advancing, not retreating, will Allah expiate my sins thereby? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you are killed in the path of Allah, patient, seeking reward, advancing, not retreating, Allah will expiate your sins thereby. Then the man remained as long as Allah willed, then said: O Messenger of Allah, if I am killed in the path of Allah, will Allah expiate my sins thereby? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you are killed in the path of Allah, patient, seeking reward, advancing, not retreating, Allah will expiate your sins thereby, except debt; thus Jibril, upon him be peace, said to me."
"23003","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammam ibn Yahya and Aban ibn Yazid informed us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the first two rakahs of Zuhr and Asr with the Fatihah of the Book and a surah, and would let us hear a verse sometimes, and would recite in the last two rakahs with the Fatihah of the Book."
"23004","Abu Said narrated to us: Harb, meaning Ibn Shaddad, narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, and he mentioned the like of it."
"23005","Rawh narrated to us: Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us: Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Qatadah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not make nabidh of rutab and zahw, and dates and raisins, together, and make nabidh of each one separately."
"23006","Yahya said: So I asked Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah about that, and he informed me, on the authority of his father, with that."
"23007","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, on the authority of Said al-Maqburi, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, on the authority of Abu Qatadah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu, then prayed at the land of Sad at the foot of the Harrah near the houses of al-Suqya, then said: O Allah, Ibrahim is Your close friend, Your servant, and Your prophet; he supplicated to You for the people of Makkah, and I, Muhammad, am Your servant, Your prophet, and Your messenger; I supplicate to You for the people of Madinah with the like of what Ibrahim supplicated to You for the people of Makkah. We supplicate to You to bless for them their sa, their mudd, and their fruits. O Allah, make Madinah beloved to us as You made Makkah beloved to us, and transfer whatever epidemic is in it to Khumm. O Allah, I have declared sacred what is between its two lava tracts, as You declared the Sanctuary sacred upon the tongue of Ibrahim."
"23008","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit: He heard Abdullah ibn Rabah narrating, on the authority of Abu Qatadah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions, when they stood for prayer and prayed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Pray it tomorrow at its time."
"23009","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Bakr, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Rabah, on the authority of Abu Qatadah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he halted to rest at night, would lie on his right side, and when he halted to rest before dawn, he would set up his forearms and place his head between his hands."
"23010","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr and Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf both said: Hisham narrated to us, he said: Yahya wrote to me that Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah narrated to him, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call is made for prayer, do not stand until you see me."
"23011","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us: Harb, meaning Ibn Shaddad, narrated to us: Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you goes to the toilet, let him not wipe himself with his right hand, and when he drinks, let him not breathe into his vessel."
"23012","Abu Said narrated to us: Harb narrated to us: Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Qatadah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees a dream that pleases him, let him narrate it, for it is glad tidings from Allah, mighty and majestic; and whoever sees a dream that he dislikes, let him not narrate it, and let him spit to his left and seek refuge in Allah from its evil."
"23013","Hammad ibn Khalid al-Khayyat narrated to us: Malik narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq ibn Abi Talhah, on the authority of Humaydah, on the authority of Kabshah, she said: I saw Abu Qatadah tilting the vessel for the cat, and it drank. He said: Do you wonder? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us: It is not impure; it is among those, male and female, who go around among you."
"23014","Mamar ibn Sulayman, he is al-Raqqi, narrated to us: al-Hajjaj narrated to us, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, on the authority of his father, that wudu water was placed for him, and a cat lapped from it, so he proceeded to perform wudu. They said: O Abu Qatadah, a cat has lapped from it. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The cat is of the household, and it is among those, male or female, who go around among you."
"23015","Hashim narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you drinks, let him not breathe into the vessel; and when one of you urinates, let him not touch his penis with his right hand; and when one of you cleans himself after relieving himself, let him not wipe himself with his right hand."
"23016","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Abu Muhammad ibn Mabad ibn Abi Qatadah informed us, on the authority of Ibn Kab ibn Malik, he said: Abu Qatadah came out to us while we were saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said such, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said such. He said: May faces be disfigured. Do you know what you are saying? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire. Affan said: And Muhammad ibn Kab said to me."
"23017","Hasan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Muhammad ibn Mabad ibn Abi Qatadah, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Kab ibn Malik narrating that Abu Qatadah went out to them, and he mentioned its meaning."
"23018","Abu Qatan said: Hisham narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah wrote to me, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not stand until you see me, meaning for prayer."
"23019","Muhammad ibn al-Nawshajan, and he is Abu Jafar al-Suwaydi, narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of al-Awzai, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst of people in theft is the one who steals from his prayer. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he steal from his prayer? He said: He does not complete its bowing nor its prostration, or he said: He does not straighten his back in bowing and prostration."
"23020","al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of al-Awzai, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"23021","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Said, he said: I heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman heard Abu Qatadah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The good dream is from Allah, and the confused dream is from Satan; so when one of you sees something he dislikes, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge in Allah from its evil, for it will not harm him."
"23022","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan: Said and Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, on the authority of Amr ibn Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Qatadah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come out carrying the daughter of Zaynab upon his neck, and would lead the people in prayer; when he bowed he put her down, and when he stood he carried her."
"23023","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah: He heard his father Abu Qatadah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade making nabidh of rutab and zahw together, or dates and raisins together, and said: Make nabidh of each one of them separately."
"23024","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us: Yahya narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, that Abu Qatadah informed him, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you drinks, let him not breathe into the vessel; and when one of you goes to the toilet, let him not clean himself with his right hand. And Abu Amir said: And let none of you touch his penis with his right hand."
"23025","Waki narrated to us: Ali, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the first two rakahs of Zuhr, letting us hear a verse sometimes; he would prolong the first rakah and shorten the second, and would recite in the first two rakahs of Asr, and would prolong the first rakah of Fajr and shorten the second."
"23026","Waki narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, my father said, and Hashim narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us, all together, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When prayer is established, do not stand until you see me, and upon you is calmness."
"23027","Waki narrated to us: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, on the authority of Ghaylan ibn Jarir, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Mabad, on the authority of Abu Qatadah, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting the day of Arafah. He said: I expect from Allah expiation for two years, past and coming. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what about a man who fasts the whole year? He said: He neither fasted nor broke fast, or: He did not fast and did not break fast. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what about a man who fasts one day and breaks fast one day? He said: That is the fast of my brother Dawud, upon him be peace. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what about a man who fasts one day and breaks fast two days? He said: I wish I were given strength for that. He said: What about a man who fasts two days and breaks fast one day? He said: And who can bear that? He said: And he was asked about fasting the day of Ashura. He said: I expect from Allah expiation for a year."
"23028","Waki narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Umaymis: Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, on the authority of al-Zuraqi, called Amr ibn Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Qatadah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray with his daughter upon his shoulder, and he said once: He carried Umamah while praying; when he intended to bow or prostrate he put her down, and when he stood he took her."
"23029","Waki narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him not sit until he prays two rakahs."
"23030","Waki narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile time, for Allah is al-Dahr."
"23031","Muhammad ibn Abi Adiy narrated to us, on the authority of al-Hajjaj, meaning Ibn Abi Uthman al-Sawwaf, on the authority of Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray with us, reciting in Zuhr and Asr in the first two rakahs with the Fatihah of the Book and two surahs, and letting us hear a verse sometimes; he would prolong the first rakah of Zuhr and shorten the second, and likewise the dawn prayer."
"23032","Muhammad ibn Abi Adiy narrated to us, on the authority of al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman al-Sawwaf, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you drinks, let him not breathe into the vessel; and when he enters the toilet, let him not wipe himself with his right hand; and when he urinates, let him not touch his penis with his right hand."
"23033","Yahya ibn Abi Kathir said: And Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats, let him not eat with his left; and when he drinks, let him not drink with his left; and when he takes, let him not take with his left; and when he gives, let him not give with his left."
"23034","Affan narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, on the authority of his father, he said: A man among us died, and we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for him to pray over him. He said: Did he leave anything? They said: No, by Allah, he left nothing. He said: Did he leave any debt upon him? They said: Yes, eighteen dirhams. He said: Did he leave payment for it? They said: No, by Allah, he left nothing for it. He said: Then you pray over him. Abu Qatadah said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I pay it on his behalf, will you pray over him? He said: If you pay it on his behalf in full, I will pray over him. He said: So Abu Qatadah went and paid it on his behalf. He said: Have you paid what was upon him? He said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for him and prayed over him."
"23035","al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, on the authority of al-Awzai: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me: Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah narrated to us: Abu Qatadah narrated to me, or: He narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two rakahs of Zuhr with the Fatihah of the Book and a surah, prolonging the first two, and in Asr the like of that, and letting us hear a verse sometimes."
